IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art72: Article 72, post-market monitoring by providers and the post-market monitoring plan for high-risk AI systems.
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Group General (Art 113 second paragraph): applies from 2 August 2026, and Art 111(2) can save a
-- high-risk AI system placed on the market earlier (aia-timeline.l4, called through P8-gate.l4).
-- Article 72(3) is the only paragraph the Omnibus changed (the `▼M1 REPLACED` block): both texts are encoded.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect (the Publications Office says so); as-enacted wording is quoted from the base file.
-- Reading a result (the brief's rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled): JUST FALSE where the text itself says no; NOTHING (not covered)
-- where the text is silent, is limited by its own wording, or the provision does not yet apply on the date asked.

DECLARE `Art 72 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 72(1) establish and document a post-market monitoring system`
    `Art 72(2) actively and systematically collect, document and analyse relevant data through the post-market monitoring system`
    `Art 72(2) include an analysis of the interaction with other AI systems in the post-market monitoring`
    `Art 72(3) base the post-market monitoring system on a post-market monitoring plan that is part of the technical documentation`
    `Art 72(3) as enacted adopt the implementing act laying down the template and the list of elements of the post-market monitoring plan`
    `Art 72(3) as amended adopt guidance, including a template, on the post-market monitoring plan`
    `Art 72(4) integrate the necessary elements into the systems and plans already existing under the Union harmonisation legislation`

§ `Article 72(1): the provider's system`

-- src:1119 | 1. Providers shall establish and document a post-market monitoring system in a manner that is proportionate to the nature of the AI technologies and the risks of the high-risk AI system.
@ref Art 72(1) (src:1119)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has established a post-market monitoring system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has documented the post-market monitoring system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the post-market monitoring system is proportionate to the nature of the AI technologies and the risks of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(1) the provider has met the duty to establish and document a post-market monitoring system` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is the duty of providers "of the high-risk AI system"
              ELSE JUST (`the provider has established a post-market monitoring system` AND `the provider has documented the post-market monitoring system` AND `the post-market monitoring system is proportionate to the nature of the AI technologies and the risks of the high-risk AI system`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers shall establish and document a post-market monitoring system in a manner that is proportionate" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The text gives it no time limit and no consequence, so no trace can show it breached
-- (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (P8)"). Nothing is owed before the group applies.
@ref Art 72(1) (src:1119)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 72 act`
`Art 72(1) the provider's duty to establish and document a post-market monitoring system` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 1
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)) OR (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`))
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked, the system is saved by Art 111(2), or the system is not high-risk
         ELSE
             PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party provider`
             MUST `Art 72(1) establish and document a post-market monitoring system`
             HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 72(2): what the system collects, and what it does not cover`

-- src:1120 | 2. The post-market monitoring system shall actively and systematically collect, document and analyse relevant data which may be provided by deployers or which may be collected through other sources on the performance of high-risk AI systems throughout their lifetime, and which allow the provider to evaluate the continuous compliance of AI systems with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2. Where relevant, post-market monitoring shall include an analysis of the interaction with other AI systems. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers which are law-enforcement authorities.
@ref Art 72(2) first sentence (src:1120)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the post-market monitoring system actively and systematically collects the relevant data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the post-market monitoring system documents the relevant data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the post-market monitoring system analyses the relevant data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is on the performance of high-risk AI systems throughout their lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data allows the provider to evaluate the continuous compliance of AI systems with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2) first sentence the post-market monitoring system collects, documents and analyses the relevant data as required` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 2
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "high-risk AI systems"
              ELSE JUST (    `the post-market monitoring system actively and systematically collects the relevant data`
                         AND `the post-market monitoring system documents the relevant data`
                         AND `the post-market monitoring system analyses the relevant data`
                         AND `the data is on the performance of high-risk AI systems throughout their lifetime`
                         AND `the data allows the provider to evaluate the continuous compliance of AI systems with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall actively and systematically collect, document and analyse relevant data" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- Second sentence: "Where relevant". When the interaction is not relevant the text asks for nothing, which is its own "where" gate (the periods ruling's rule (b)).
@ref Art 72(2) second sentence (src:1120)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an analysis of the interaction with other AI systems is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2) second sentence the post-market monitoring must include an analysis of the interaction with other AI systems` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 2
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about post-market monitoring of high-risk AI systems
              ELSE IF `an analysis of the interaction with other AI systems is relevant`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where relevant" (the unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a)/(b)) (fork F-72-2-second-duty)

