@ref Art 72(3), both versions (src:1122)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 72 act`
`Art 72(3) the Commission's duty to adopt the template for the post-market monitoring plan` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 72(3) as enacted the Commission's duty to adopt the implementing act with the template`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 72(3) as amended the Commission's duty to adopt the guidance including a template`  -- VERSION as amended

§ `Article 72(4): the choice to integrate into an existing sectoral system`

-- src:1124 | 4. For high-risk AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, where a post-market monitoring system and plan are already established under that legislation, in order to ensure consistency, avoid duplications and minimise additional burdens, providers shall have a choice of integrating, as appropriate, the necessary elements described in paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 using the template referred in paragraph 3 into systems and plans already existing under that legislation, provided that it achieves an equivalent level of protection.
-- src:1125 | The first subparagraph of this paragraph shall also apply to high-risk AI systems referred to in point 5 of Annex III placed on the market or put into service by financial institutions that are subject to requirements under Union financial services law regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes.
@ref Art 72(4) (src:1124-1125)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a post-market monitoring system and plan are already established under that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the integration achieves an equivalent level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(4) first subparagraph the provider may integrate the necessary elements into the systems and plans already existing under the Union harmonisation legislation` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 4
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT `the high-risk AI system is covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is for "high-risk AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))
              ELSE IF NOT `a post-market monitoring system and plan are already established under that legislation`
                   THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a post-market monitoring system and plan are already established under that legislation" (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-72-4-where)
                   ELSE IF `the integration achieves an equivalent level of protection`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided that it achieves an equivalent level of protection" limits the choice; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING for a failed proviso of a power (fork F-72-4-proviso)

@ref Art 72(4) second subparagraph (src:1125)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system referred to in point 5 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is placed on the market or put into service by a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial institution is subject to requirements under Union financial services law regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(4) second subparagraph the first subparagraph also applies to the high-risk AI system of a financial institution` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 4
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF       `the AI system is a high-risk AI system referred to in point 5 of Annex III`
                   AND `the AI system is placed on the market or put into service by a financial institution`
                   AND `the financial institution is subject to requirements under Union financial services law regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall also apply" extends the first subparagraph to these systems only; for others the first subparagraph speaks for itself

-- The choice as a regulative rule: a permission with no time limit and no consequence (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (P8)").
@ref Art 72(4) first subparagraph (src:1124)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 72 act`
`Art 72(4) the provider's choice to integrate into the systems and plans already existing` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 72 4
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is offered: the group does not apply on the date asked, or the system is saved by Art 111(2)
         ELSE
             PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party provider`
             MAY `Art 72(4) integrate the necessary elements into the systems and plans already existing under the Union harmonisation legislation`
             HENCE FULFILLED
